  "id": "68",
  "name": "Real estate activities",
  "section": "M",
  "summary": "In real estate filings AI is first a demand driver: data-centre landlords and developers report hyperscale leasing, power-constrained markets and AI workloads, while office and industrial owners cite leasing by AI companies. Own use centres on automated valuation, algorithmic rent pricing (with antitrust and fair-housing exposure), AI leasing assistants, tenant screening and smart-building energy optimisation; brokers and portals face AI search disintermediation. Risks named include tenant concentration in hyperscalers, AI overbuild, grid constraints, and deepfake or impersonation fraud in property transactions.",
